    notes: "The beltpack mic input is UNBALANCED: Clear-Com states that pin 1 \u201cmic signal low\u201d is actually signal ground, and RTS/Telex tie the dynamic-mic \u2212 leg to ground to unbalance it \u2014 that is what the pin 3 \u2192 pin 1 jumper does. The mic ground is pin 1, never pin 3 (pin 3 is the earphone return \u2014 grounding the mic there injects the earphone return current into the mic circuit). Dynamic mics only: intercom headset mics are often electrets powered by a DC bias the pack puts on pin 2 \u2014 set the pack's mic switch to DYNAMIC for an XLR3 dynamic mic, and never expect a phantom-powered condenser to work here. The pack's headset jack is a female XLR5, so this cable needs a MALE XLR5 and a FEMALE XLR3. Never let a party-line cable's male end, or the pack's male LINE LOOP jack, meet this adapter's female XLR3 \u2014 30 V DC on pin 2 would go straight into the pack's mic input. Dynamic MICROPHONE only \u2014 never plug a mixer or playback OUTPUT into the female XLR3: the pin 3\u2192pin 1 jumper shorts that output's cold leg to ground (Rane 151). To feed program into the pack build a separate padded leg with pin 3 floated. Face/solder: the app draws the FEMALE mating face. For a MALE cable end that drawing is exactly what the male insert's solder cups look like, so wire the male straight from the FACE VIEW. For a FEMALE cable end use the app's SOLDER SIDE view (the mirror).",
