    notes: "Use the + button to add more XLR channels. Each XLR cable gets its own channel on the DT12. Pin layout follows the Clark Wire DT12 table. Clark itself warns that not every manufacturer follows it, and 37-pin FK-37 shells are also used for 16-channel snakes with other pinouts \u2014 confirm the far end before trusting a channel map. Channel 1 uses pins 5, 6 and 1; the remaining pins 2\u20134 and 7\u201336 belong to channels 2\u201312 and go live as you add channels; only pin 37 is spare. The DT12 face drawing in the app is schematic (channel groups), not the FK-37 insert geometry \u2014 count pins by the moulded numbers on the insert. Phantom from the far end of the snake reaches XLR3 pins 2/3 on every tail \u2014 switch 48 V off on channels fed by line-level sources, DIs or wireless receivers that do not want it. If any snake channel is carrying Clear-Com/RTS party line, its tail has +30 VDC on XLR3 pin 2 \u2014 label that tail at both ends, never plug a mic or DI into it, and never patch it into a phantom-powered input.",
