    notes: "StudioHub+ receive side. Pair with TRS\u2192RJ45 at the source. Official StudioHub+ carries the Sleeve on the cable shield (pin 4 = DC GND, pin 5 = n/c); PinRef uses pins 4/5 as ground so unshielded Cat5 works, which only holds if the far end matches. Pins 7\u20138 carry \u00b115 V DC on powered StudioHub+ panels; never plug into an Ethernet/PoE port or any intercom RJ45 (HelixNet puts \u00b130 V on pins 3\u20138, i.e. on the Sleeve and on ch2 Tip/Ring). If the TRS end goes into an unbalanced TS jack, the jack shorts Ring (RJ45 2 = the source's cold leg) to ground over the whole run \u2014 fine for transformer/cross-coupled sources, bad for a plain op-amp output; use an XLR3\u2192TS or TRS\u2192TS adapter that floats cold instead. If the run originates from a party line, +30 V DC arrives on the Tip. The TRS plug fits a 1/4\" SPEAKER output as well as a line input \u2014 never plug it into one; speaker level would travel down the Cat5 into the far-end source.",
