    notes: "\u26a0\ufe0f DANGER \u2014 camera triax carries the CCU power supply on the CENTRE conductor (Sony: 180 V DC) with the inner shield as its return. Before using a triax run as SDI coax, physically disconnect BOTH ends from any CCU, base station or camera \u2014 a run with a CCU on it is live at up to 180 V DC. NEVER plug this adapter into a CCU or camera triax port. This is the end a tech plugs into the wall plate or patch \u2014 if that run is live from a CCU, 180 V DC lands on the SDI input. Inner shield is the 75 \u03a9 return; outer shield bonded so nothing floats (earlier PinRef revisions did the opposite). Only 75 \u03a9 broadcast triax (Belden 1857A; 9232 is discontinued but common in the ground; Canare L-5CFTX \u2014 LV-77S is a coax). Keep identical to the corrected BNC \u2192 Triax build. Triax connector family must match the plant: Sony ships Kings-type in the US/Canada and Fischer 1051 elsewhere, and Lemo is also common \u2014 they do not intermate.",
