    notes: "Straight-through is correct for an extension and for Tascam ANALOG device-to-device. Any AES/EBU DB25 device-to-device cable \u2014 Tascam OR Yamaha format \u2014 must cross IN to OUT (Tascam: pins 12, 24 and 25 land on 6, 18 and 19 at the other end; Yamaha: inputs 1\u20134/14\u201317 meet outputs 5\u20138/18\u201321) \u2014 a straight male-to-male between two AES devices ties outputs to outputs and passes nothing. Straight-through is only for extensions and Tascam ANALOG device-to-device; Tascam\u2194Yamaha needs a purpose-built conversion cable (Hosa). Tascam analog and Yamaha AES use the same shell: a straight cable is the one thing that lets a phantom-powered analog mic pre meet a digital card, so label snakes by format. Not for RS-232 (DTE-to-DTE needs a null modem) \u2014 keep audio DB25s away from serial and parallel ports. For AES/EBU use build the extension from 110 \u03a9 digital multipair (or keep it very short); analog snake cable is fine only for the analog case.",
