    notes: "XLR4 mic is unbalanced. Per Rane Note 151 Figure 5 (column 2, row e \u2014 Unbalanced Output \u2192 Balanced Input, off-the-shelf-cable wiring), tie the destination XLR3 pin 3 (Cold) to pin 1 (Ground) at the XLR3 connector. This gives the balanced input's diff-amp a proper ground reference. Earphone signal is not tapped here \u2014 mic-only. Works with DYNAMIC headset mics; electret headset mics need the DC bias a beltpack puts on pin 2 and will be silent into a mixer. Never turn on 48 V phantom into this cable \u2014 pin 3 is grounded here and the capsule is not built for it. Genders: a Clear-Com headset has a female XLR4 and a mixer mic input is a female XLR3, so this adapter is MALE XLR4 to MALE XLR3; for a Telex PH-88R (male XLR4) the XLR4 end must be female. Mixer mic input only \u2014 never into an intercom LINE / party-line jack: 30 V DC on pin 2 would drive ~150 mA through the headset's 200 \u03a9 dynamic capsule and the pin 3\u2192pin 1 tie would short the line's audio to ground.",
