    notes: "Check BOTH ends before using a 4-conductor cable: Neutrik's suggested cabinet wiring for \u2018standard PA\u2019 and bridged-mono speakers ties 2+ to 1\u2212 inside the cabinet, and some amplifiers put a second channel (or a bridged output) on 2\u00b1 of one socket \u2014 two channels on one socket into such a cabinet shorts Ch2+ to Ch1\u2212 and can destroy the amp. Polarity convention (Neutrik): + is in phase, lower numbers = lower frequencies. Speaker level only \u2014 speakON is NOT an AC mains or power connector (Neutrik), and it has no rated breaking capacity: mute or power down the amp before mating or unmating under drive. Face drawing: the app's speakON diamond orientation is UNVERIFIED (set from a physical reference; one reviewer reads it as the solder-side order rotated 45\u00b0) \u2014 wire from the moulded 1+/1\u2212/2+/2\u2212 marks on the insert, never from pin positions in the picture. Never run this lead between two amplifier OUTPUT sockets \u2014 amp outputs and cabinet inputs are the same chassis socket, and two outputs tied together can destroy either amp.",
