    notes: "Ring is tied to Sleeve at the TRS end for proper unbalanced operation. ~12 dB level difference expected (consumer \u221210 dBV to pro +4 dBu); the balanced input's gain makes it up. Direction matters: this is physically identical to the TRS\u2192RCA build but with Ring tied to Sleeve. Used backwards (balanced TRS OUTPUT into an RCA input) the jumper grounds the output's cold leg \u2014 use the TRS\u2192RCA build for that direction and label this one RCA\u2192TRS. Never plug the TRS end into a stereo headphone or stereo aux OUTPUT \u2014 Ring is grounded here and would short that device's right-channel amplifier.",
