    notes: "Cable Wholesale grey shell, 4 wires. Pairing is right for RS-422: TX+/TX\u2212 (DE-9 3/8) share RJ45 3/6 and RX+/RX\u2212 (DE-9 7/2) share RJ45 4/5. No common is carried (Kalypso DE-9 pin 6), so it relies on both chassis sharing a ground \u2014 fine between co-grounded racks. The RS-232 half of the old title was wrong: RS-232 is single-ended and needs pin 5; this shell has no ground conductor at all. The app's DE-9 face shows RS-232 names (RxD/TxD/RTS/CTS) \u2014 ignore them; the descriptions carry the RS-422 signals. Shells 79\u201382 look identical: record the colour on each and never pair an RS-232 shell (81/82) with an RS-422 shell (79/80) on one Cat5 \u2014 RS-232 levels (\u00b112 V) exceed an RS-422 receiver's \u00b17 V common-mode rating. Never plug the RJ45 into an Ethernet/PoE port or a HelixNet powerline jack (\u00b130 V on RJ45 3\u20138 would sit across the RS-422 driver and receiver pins). Kalypso end: Serial 1\u20138 / CPL (RS-422) ONLY \u2014 never the Diagnostic D-9 (same female D-9 on the same frame), whose pins 2 and 7 are \u00b112 V RS-232 outputs that would land on the far RS-422 receiver's bus pins (absolute maximum \u221210 V). Straight-through Cat5 patch only: a crossover cable moves the TX pair (RJ45 3/6) onto 1/2, where the far shell has nothing.",
