    notes: "\u26a0\ufe0f UNVERIFIED. Only 3 wires and DE-9 pin 5 (RS-232 signal ground) is NOT carried; the old note's \u2018ground through connector shell or cable shield\u2019 does not exist on a plastic Cable Wholesale shell with UTP Cat5. A 3-wire RS-232 link is TxD, RxD and ground. The pin-1 wire (labelled DCD) can only be a ground if the far port has chassis ground on pin 1 (Sony-style RS-422 ports do; the Kalypso's only RS-232 port, the Diagnostic D-9, has DCD \u2014 an output \u2014 on pin 1), so at the Kalypso Diagnostic port there is NO ground path as recorded. Fix: add DE-9 pin 5 \u2192 RJ45 pin 7 (brown pair, next to the pin-8 wire) at both shells and drop DCD, or confirm from the far device's manual that its pin 1 is chassis ground and relabel the wire. Kalypso end: Diagnostic D-9 ONLY \u2014 Serial 1\u20138 are RS-422 and \u00b112 V RS-232 on their pins 2/3 exceeds their rating (default tally port is Serial 5). Not Yost/Cisco-compatible (those carry ground on RJ45 4/5 where this shell has data). Never into an Ethernet/PoE port or a HelixNet jack (this shell sits on the PoE Mode-B pairs 4/5 and 7/8). TxD and RxD share one twisted pair (blue 4/5), which invites crosstalk on long runs. Note the Kalypso HD/Duo frame's only RS-232 port is the D-9 Diagnostic port (DCE: 1 DCD, 2 TX, 3 RX, 5 GND); its Serial 1\u20138 ports are RS-422 \u2014 record which port this plugs into. Shells 79\u201382 look identical: label by colour and never mix an RS-232 shell with the RS-422 shells on one Cat5. Never into a StudioHub+/Axia RJ45 panel: its brown pair carries 15 V\u2212 on pin 7 and 15 V+ on pin 8 \u2014 this shell's DCD wire, and the ground wire the fix above would add. The Kalypso Diagnostic port is DCE (TX on pin 2, RX on pin 3), so against a DTE device this straight shell pair is the right one of the two; the null shell is not.",
